+# Studio expansion — local checkpoint, 2026-10-11
+
+At 18:38 UTC this is a **partial local implementation**, not a completed implementation of all four requested areas and not a deployment. The live backend remains on the previously deployed product-telemetry release. Guest coverage remains unavailable. Local car dirt/washing state is not collected.
+
+| Area / requirement | Implemented here | Still missing |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Client quality — BMT-018, BMT-070 | Signed-in frame histograms by configured build ID, platform/device class and scene; bounded 1 Hz spatial/segment observations; Android API 30+ crash/native-crash/ANR **process-exit reasons**; prepared Studio views. | Crash stacks/symbolication/grouping, actual device models/OS/GPU tiers, per-race/biome summaries and load-failure instrumentation, Play vitals and correct crash-free denominators. Existing build version is not a unique artifact fingerprint. |
+| Enhanced capture — BMT-053 | Routine capture is bounded to counters and sampled cells. | **Consented, expiring enhanced diagnostic capture is not implemented.** Routine counters must not be described as fulfilling BMT-053. |
+| Billing/ads — BMT-040, BMT-043 | Isolated Play ProductPurchaseV2 verification adapter and AdMob ECDSA proof verifier, with offline adversarial tests. No new dependencies. | Production package/product configuration, BillingClient integration, durable encrypted token/acknowledgement/consume jobs, RTDN authentication, reward intents/callback fulfillment and consent/placement setup. These adapters have no exposed purchase/grant endpoint. |
+| Revenue/ledger — BMT-041, BMT-044, BMT-048 | Existing development controls are preserved. No catalog price is treated as revenue. | Real spend/estimated-net/reconciled-receipt feeds, original currency/FX/tax/fee basis, void/refund reconciliation, reversal ordering/tombstones and complete entitlement projection ledger. **These are not implemented in this checkpoint.** |
+| Tracks/competition — BMT-030, BMT-032, BMT-034, BMT-036 | Per-version observed exposures/selections; latest 100 creator versions and publication state; sampled heatmap; dedicated rivalry/challenge inspector with pinned contracts, roster context, accepted-run/ticket/board/window checks, stored-best versus evidence-derived ranks/points, exact target and attempt-state window. | Complete discovery journey/visibility concentration/creator-return diagnostics; spatial collision/quit/rewind measures; historical validator phases; original evidence for archived bests lacking run links; reward delivery. Existing Product analytics retains ordered creator/external-racer cohorts. |
+| Support/moderation — BMT-033, BMT-050 | Cases, ordered append-only events, notes, issue references, revision fencing, permanent command dedupe, signed-in report/appeal API, case-linked track quarantine/restoration and audit linkage. Player report responses exclude staff notes and internal staff-created cases. | In-game report UI, record-level quarantine, automatic quarantine expiry, individual staff SSO/MFA, dedicated verified recovery and production compensation. Existing Google sign-in retains its original identity checks; no new account merging or impersonation is offered. |
+
+The moderation scope here changes track visibility and new-ticket availability through the existing hidden-track contract. It does not delete content, remove submitted evidence, rewrite accepted results or transfer balances. Restoration refuses a different owning case or intervening visibility moderation; ambiguous same-second moderation is conservatively refused. Cases use shared owner/analyst credential roles, not individual staff attribution.
+
+Competition reads use one consistent transaction, at most 200 members/5 slots/1,000 bests and the first 500 linked attempts in deterministic order. They never fetch proof/ghost objects or invoke the verifier. Creator source runs deliberately seeded into challenges remain valid without a challenge-ticket binding. A corrupt linked source remains visible rather than silently becoming an accepted rank. Archived timing alone cannot prove original acceptance. Current points are explained using the existing rivalry policy; reads never change official scores.
+
+Network and compute:
+
+- Reuse the existing authenticated, account/origin-separated durable telemetry outbox: 50 events / 64 KiB per packet, 1,000 events / 2 MiB local queue, stable-ID retries and acknowledgement after commit. A backend feature flag plus negotiated `quality_schema_version=1` is required. `BMT_CLIENT_QUALITY_ENABLED` defaults false and requires telemetry enabled.
+- Frames become eight integer buckets every five minutes, separated by menu/race/editor scene. No per-frame requests or stored frame arrays. Spatial sampling reads presentation state once a second, using 20 m cells / 32 route segments and retaining the 16 lowest stable cell hashes per ten-minute window. It is censored sampled presence, not total dwell time, distinct drivers or validated race evidence. Inclusion probabilities are unavailable; local dropped-cell counts are not currently projected to Studio.
+- Quality events are passive for the existing five-minute idle flush rule. They do not trigger one-minute journey flushes; actual product activity retains its original cadence. No transport or persistence worker starts during an ordinary foreground race; pooled identifiers reserve 32 entries for product/race observations. Extended races may lose optional counters when the pool/outbox budget is exhausted.
+- The Windows collector fixture measured **1.0034 µs/frame** and **18.472 µs/cell observation**. Its 19-event compact packet was **5,852 bytes**. A single-scene hour has at most 12 frame summaries and 96 retained-cell summaries, plus at most four startup exit observations. Packet size and collector timing are measured; hourly body traffic, TLS/radio cost and physical-device CPU remain unmeasured. Retries, existing product traffic and compressed transport affect actual traffic.
+- The existing lower-priority product worker performs grouped counter upserts in the same bounded projection transaction. No new worker instance, simulation, geometry scan or object download is introduced. Diagnostic facts use 64-bit counters and paced retention under the existing fact retention setting. Studio reads prepared counters with a 1,000-row response ceiling; it does not scan raw events. New indexed ordering supports recent creator/rivalry/challenge lists. Two small API reads serve each new workspace: context (no operational count queries) and its bounded data query. Large-population query load has not been benchmarked for this slice.
+- Android reads at most four OS exit records, once outside racing, with a persisted cursor. It uploads the reason and collection time; the original exit timestamp stays in the local cursor. It never reads trace streams, PIDs, device IDs, raw logs or credentials. These describe the previous process and cannot prove a crash affected the current signed-in account. API availability is documented by [Android ApplicationExitInfo](https://developer.android.com/reference/android/app/ApplicationExitInfo).
+
+Provider contracts follow [Google Play ProductPurchaseV2](https://developers.google.com/android-publisher/api-ref/rest/v3/purchases.productsv2) and [AdMob SSV](https://developers.google.com/admob/android/ssv). The Play adapter checks explicit package, exact product, server account binding, quantity, state, completion time and refundable quantity; pending/test/refund state stays explicit. AdMob matches [Google's reference verifier](https://github.com/tink-crypto/tink-java-apps/blob/main/rewardedads/src/main/java/com/google/crypto/tink/apps/rewardedads/RewardedAdsVerifier.java): percent-decode the URI query once, preserve literal plus signs and parameter order, then authenticate before parsing business fields. It rejects duplicate/unknown parameters and unsupported rewards, and caches trusted Google EC keys for one hour with paced refresh. Signature validation alone never grants resumes: configured placement, server-issued intent, expiry, permanent transaction dedupe and atomic fulfillment are still required. No production provider call, purchase, ad grant or payout was performed.
+
+Actual validation:
+
+- `.tools/backend-venv/Scripts/python.exe scripts/test_studio_expansion_postgres.py` — **116 passed, 2 skipped**, 96.33 s, owned PostgreSQL 17 removed. Covers additive migrations through `0027_client_quality`, duplicate/concurrent ingestion and projection, concurrent case creation/edit fencing, and touched Studio/product/store regressions. Skips are SQLite variants that require PostgreSQL row locks; corresponding PostgreSQL paths run. Existing Starlette/httpx deprecation warning remains.
+- Final focused SQLite/domain/proof tests — **10 passed**, 6.62 s, including internal-case privacy and stored-rank/source inconsistency checks. Ruff checks on all touched/new backend source, migrations, tests and harnesses passed.
+- `powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 -Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_client_quality.gd` — **26 checks / zero failures**, including finite bucket boundaries, bounded spatial memory, lack of exact positions/device IDs and a nonempty durable-event packet.
+- Same entry point with `res://tests/test_product_telemetry.gd` — **55 checks / zero failures**. Existing queue/identity/retry/storage tests retain their assertions.
+- `.tools/backend-venv/Scripts/python.exe scripts/test_studio_expansion_console.py` — **9 browser checks passed**, actual headless Edge against a newly owned, seeded loopback database; owner creation/note/quarantine, HTML escaping, histograms/heatmap/exact target, analyst read-only access, 390 px capture and zero JavaScript errors. [Browser receipt](evidence/studio-expansion-2026-10-11/browser.json), [case capture](evidence/studio-expansion-2026-10-11/cases-desktop.png), [histogram](evidence/studio-expansion-2026-10-11/quality-desktop.png), [heatmap](evidence/studio-expansion-2026-10-11/heatmap-desktop.png), [competition](evidence/studio-expansion-2026-10-11/competition-desktop.png), [mobile](evidence/studio-expansion-2026-10-11/competition-mobile.png). These are test records, not live populations or completed canonical races.
+- Pinned Godot `CheckScript` passed. `ExportAndroid` parsed **530 scripts**, then its full validation stopped at the creator-v22 pine geometry golden assertion (**113 creator checks, one failure**). Expected fixture was not changed. Log: `build/logs/ExportAndroid-672/creator-tests.log`. **No new APK was produced by this attempt**, and a full regression pass is not claimed.
+- JDK 17 `javac -Xlint:all` against installed Android 36 compiled `BmtProcessExits.java` successfully to the owned workspace classes directory (1,819-byte class). This checks the adapter's Java/API compatibility, not full plugin packaging or device behavior. The first sandboxed compiler attempt emitted SDK access errors; only the subsequent successful escalated run is accepted.
+- No phone/device test, live deployment, live database migration, account recovery, production compensation or provider fulfillment was performed. Local schema additions are not applied to the deployed backend.
